<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GFSA's Black Mountain Dec qtr net profit rises.</title>
<headline>GFSA's Black Mountain Dec qtr net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Dec versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending 18.47 vs 15.87</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  2.64 vs  3.18</p>
<p>    Sales					91.59 vs 68.79</p>
<p>    Ore milled (tonnes)		  367,000 vs 379,000</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates produced (tonnes, unless stated):</p>
<p>    - Copper				   1,173 vs 1,309</p>
<p>    - Lead				    20,937 vs 20,495</p>
<p>    - Silver (kg)			   24,291 vs 26,380</p>
<p>    - Zinc				     7,289 vs 7,821</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates sold (tonnes, unless stated):</p>
<p>    - Copper				   2,630 vs 250</p>
<p>    - Lead				    19,929 vs 21,714</p>
<p>    - Silver (kg)			   27,843 vs 25,110</p>
<p>    - Zinc				     8,164 vs 7,390</p>
<p>Full name: Black Mountain Mineral Development Co (Pty) Ltd, managed by Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
